nd{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular\n- $C$ is lower triangular\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${C}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "dff7fd68dacf0f385d9535782d42479a0e621010e338f5467a2c36beed07ea6b" "basis" 1474 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacade