ation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${c}_{12}=1\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Diagonal matrix"] ["text" "Identity matrix"] ["text" "Lower triangular matrix"] ["text" "Other"] ["text" "Upper triangular matrix"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Upper triangular matrix"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-74316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-42090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are lower triangular matrices since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrix $C$ is *not* a lower triangular matrix since it has a non-zero element above the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =-2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67da902cfd1a30702c40e7a639203"} {"question" "q-126351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66708c2f91a5a0d7798b7042acc394991fc9eb566947eed6c18c02af47ef0f76"} {"question" "q-126351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/state.json" "file_sha256" "8edd8052848e399de5497f12c3bb0d4ee5a67d